{"name":"Gold Digger","hex":"#d1b075","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"gold digger","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Someone who digs or mines for gold.","A person, especially a woman, who cultivates a personal relationship with someone in order to attain wealth."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gold_digger"}],"entries":[{"title":"The Gold Diggers (1923 film)","blocks":[{"text":"The Gold Diggers is a Warner Bros. silent comedy film directed by Harry Beaumont with screenplay by Grant Carpenter based on the play The Gold Diggers by Avery Hopwood which ran for 282 performances on Broadway in 1919 and 1920. Both the play and the film were produced by David Belasco. The film stars Hope Hampton, Wyndham Standing, and Louise Fazenda. It was also the (uncredited) film debut of Louise Beavers."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Gold_Diggers_%28SAYRE_14187%29.jpg/330px-Gold_Diggers_%28SAYRE_14187%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Gold_Diggers_(1923_film)","wikidata":"Q3987302"},{"title":"Gold Diggers of Broadway","blocks":[{"text":"Gold Diggers of Broadway is a 1929 American sound (All-Talking) pre-Code musical comedy film directed by Roy Del Ruth and starring Winnie Lightner and Nick Lucas. Distributed by Warner Bros. Pictures, the film is the second all-talking, all-Technicolor feature-length film."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Gold_Diggers_of_Broadway_%281929%29_Window_Card.jpg/330px-Gold_Diggers_of_Broadway_%281929%29_Window_Card.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gold_Diggers_of_Broadway","wikidata":"Q3110003"},{"title":"Gold Digger (Kanye West song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Gold Digger\" is a song by the American rapper Kanye West featuring the American singer Jamie Foxx, from West's second studio album, Late Registration (2005). The song includes additional vocals from Plain Pat and Don C. West created the beat in Atlanta. He and Jon Brion produced the song. It was originally set to be recorded for Shawnna's debut studio album, Worth Tha Weight (2004), but the song was later passed on to West. On July 5, 2005, it was released to American rhythmic contemporary radio stations by Roc-A-Fella and Def Jam as the second single from West's album. The song set a record for the most digital downloads in a week, selling over 80,000."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/62/Gold_Digger.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gold_Digger_(Kanye_West_song)","wikidata":"Q2628090"},{"title":"Gold digger","blocks":[{"text":"A gold digger is a person who engages in a type of transactional sexual relationship for money and social status rather than love. If it turns into marriage, it is a type of marriage of convenience."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/JudgeMagazine24Jul1920.jpg/330px-JudgeMagazine24Jul1920.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gold_digger","wikidata":"Q10290445"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Photoplay_-_1929.11_-_54_-_Gold_Diggers_of_Broadway.png/330px-Photoplay_-_1929.11_-_54_-_Gold_Diggers_of_Broadway.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Photoplay_-_1929.11_-_54_-_Gold_Diggers_of_Broadway.png/330px-Photoplay_-_1929.11_-_54_-_Gold_Diggers_of_Broadway.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Image from Photoplay magazine","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APhotoplay_-_1929.11_-_54_-_Gold_Diggers_of_Broadway.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.o